            <ArticleTitle>Myophosphorylase deficiency: an unusually severe form with myoglobinuria.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>409-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myophosphorylase deficiency (McArdle disease) is characterized by exercise intolerance that usually starts in childhood. Severe cramps and myoglobinuria are rarely problems in children. We describe an 8-year-old boy with exercise-induced myoglobinuria; he was homozygous for the mutation most commonly encountered in patients with typical McArdle disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
